        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "6e21bcdb-d221-3be8-8f1a-27cf6646342e",
                "word": "alarmiste",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "363b4d0e-4248-400f-af59-66a454d6b0fe",
                        "entry_id": "6e21bcdb-d221-3be8-8f1a-27cf6646342e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "alarmistes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ecdfba4a-9907-34c9-bbab-1bb2f29d973b",
                        "entry_id": "6e21bcdb-d221-3be8-8f1a-27cf6646342e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Personne qui se plaît à répandre des bruits alarmants."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9013a22c-75eb-4163-9afa-bc95b1887ba4",
                                "sense_id": "ecdfba4a-9907-34c9-bbab-1bb2f29d973b",
                                "text": "Nul ne croyait au 30 juillet que la guerre fût proche, et lorsque quelqu'un se hasardait à faire part de ses inquiétudes, il était considéré comme un alarmiste, suspect pour le moins de jouer à la baisse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b28a6fde-8e92-4565-9e96-fd62c673ff6d",
                                "sense_id": "ecdfba4a-9907-34c9-bbab-1bb2f29d973b",
                                "text": "Le carnage, sous la figure d'un géant, tenait une coupe de sang qu'il buvait à longs traits, et un glaive à deux tranchans, sur lequel étaient gravés ces mots: Guerre à mort aux aristocrates aux modérés, aux ci-devant nobles aux prétres, aux alarmistes aux indulgens au peuple qui parle et à celui qui se-tait."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eb420ee9-41d0-4db4-9d72-4415f39e26c4",
                        "source_entry_id": "6e21bcdb-d221-3be8-8f1a-27cf6646342e",
                        "source_sense_id": "ecdfba4a-9907-34c9-bbab-1bb2f29d973b",
                        "target_lang_word": "scaremonger",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "scaremonger",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e170948-d1ad-3591-9711-4b3b8c9d788a",
                                        "entry_id": "ee0dcfa8-8025-3467-ad39-face8bc66059",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who spreads worrying rumours or needlessly alarms people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5dfcb65b-8c98-418b-9bc2-af581168b41f",
                                                "sense_id": "1e170948-d1ad-3591-9711-4b3b8c9d788a",
                                                "text": "I have refrained from giving actual names and dates, for obvious reasons, and have therefore been compelled, even at the risk of being again denounced as a scaremonger, to present the facts in the form of fiction—fiction which, I trust, will point its own patriotic moral."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "scaremonger",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6dba3683-48de-39fe-80da-9d98f4e8d247",
                                        "entry_id": "89936a4a-ecaa-3ec2-b356-effa78e4c52c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spread worrying rumours."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7804fa0-63a7-4875-8581-2e89d3b5c2ef",
                                                "sense_id": "6dba3683-48de-39fe-80da-9d98f4e8d247",
                                                "text": "We're not scaremongering / This is really happening, happening"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "150867d9-f6f7-48bc-b397-e9e27d02e6df",
                                                "sense_id": "6dba3683-48de-39fe-80da-9d98f4e8d247",
                                                "text": "If no new cases come from the Buff Club exposure site, it will be hard to believe politicians scaremongering that the delta variant is so infectious that all you have to do is walk past an infected person to get it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "20276d1e-14ed-42ae-96e2-82fc89e4efd7",
                        "source_entry_id": "6e21bcdb-d221-3be8-8f1a-27cf6646342e",
                        "source_sense_id": "ecdfba4a-9907-34c9-bbab-1bb2f29d973b",
                        "target_lang_word": "fearmonger",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fearmonger",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e92beca-f33c-360c-b109-8809bb41c306",
                                        "entry_id": "e547456c-31ab-32e8-8945-3ec01b82b373",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who spreads fear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "251b5304-f69a-4faf-b405-ef396af41b42",
                                                "sense_id": "6e92beca-f33c-360c-b109-8809bb41c306",
                                                "text": "I think the Tea Partiers, despite their contradictions, are not all wrong about Big Government. But I worry that, in time, a clever fearmonger could manipulate popular opinion into an electoral mandate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fearmonger",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "452c0834-0644-30ae-a810-bb0ba2661b8f",
                                        "entry_id": "1c02889e-4522-3b4d-a6b9-63f838e2da7c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spread fear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f5dda178-15c4-4253-9965-5b0112676f48",
                        "source_entry_id": "6e21bcdb-d221-3be8-8f1a-27cf6646342e",
                        "source_sense_id": "ecdfba4a-9907-34c9-bbab-1bb2f29d973b",
                        "target_lang_word": "alarmist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alarmist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15a96bbd-c796-347b-9ac8-313745251987",
                                        "entry_id": "e1c353fd-8896-3464-8e1d-34fdfa73133b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who causes others to become alarmed without cause."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ee2edc2-7224-4f0d-9c4a-eeca301d09b7",
                                                "sense_id": "15a96bbd-c796-347b-9ac8-313745251987",
                                                "text": "I don't mean to be an alarmist, but I do think you should prepare yourself for the worst."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19804515-c64a-413d-8b1e-b765f98403f3",
                                                "sense_id": "15a96bbd-c796-347b-9ac8-313745251987",
                                                "text": "No German troops were mobilized along Canada's border last week, no Canadian cities had been bombed, and only by the remotest flight of fancy could alarmists see the Dominion as a battleground."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "alarmist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f46d1d21-6b25-3826-9c52-4653f191be71",
                                        "entry_id": "e5ff8d87-4b7f-3719-84c0-1706ef49b78d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to causing others to become alarmed without cause."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64c76fae-98ce-4ff2-9695-6d6044c09fe4",
                                                "sense_id": "f46d1d21-6b25-3826-9c52-4653f191be71",
                                                "text": "This deliberately alarmist scaremongery has since been repeated on various occasions, notably in Brazil before 1964 and in Chile under Allende."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8d5672f6-50d1-4421-bef7-3583370d0949",
                        "source_entry_id": "6e21bcdb-d221-3be8-8f1a-27cf6646342e",
                        "source_sense_id": "ecdfba4a-9907-34c9-bbab-1bb2f29d973b",
